  "title": "Prayers for the Nights of Ramazan",
  "data": "The First Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) fifteen times.\n\nThe Second Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) twenty times.\n\nThe Third Night Prayer: Ten units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) fifty times.\n\nThe Fourth Night Prayer: Eight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) twenty times.\n\nThe Fifth Night Prayer: Two units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) fifty times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated one hundred times:\n\nThe Sixth Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Mulk](A71) (No. 67).\n\nThe Seventh Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) thirteen times.\n\nThe Eighth Night Prayer: Two units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten times. After accomplishment, SUBHANA ALLAH is repeated one thousand times:\n\nThe Ninth Night Prayer: Six units offered between the Maghrib and Isha’ obligatory Prayers with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) seven times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated fifty times:\n\nThe Tenth Night Prayer: Twenty units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) thirty times.\n\nThe Eleventh Night Prayer: Two units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) (No. 108) twenty times.\n\nThe Twelfth Night Prayer: Eight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) thirty times.\n\nThe Thirteenth Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty-five times.\n\nThe Fourteenth Night Prayer: Six units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) (No. 99) thirty times.\n\nThe Fifteenth Night Prayer: Four units; in the first two units, [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) repeated one hundred times. In the last two units, [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) repeated fifty times.\n\nThe Sixteenth Night Prayer: Twelve units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Takathur](A106) (No. 102) twelve times.\n\nThe Seventeenth Night Prayer: Two units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and any selected Surah in the first unit and [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times. After accomplishment, LA ILAHA ILLA ALLAH is repeated one hundred times:\n\nThe Eighteenth Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) twenty-five times.\n\nThe Nineteenth Night Prayer: Fifty units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) (No. 99).\n\nThe Twentieth to Twenty-Fourth Nights Prayer: At these nights, it is recommended to offer an eight unit prayer with any selected Surahs.\n\nThe Twenty-Fifth Night Prayer: Eight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten times.\n\nThe Twenty-Sixth Night Prayer: Eight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times.\n\nThe Twenty-Seventh Night Prayer: Four units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Mulk](A71). If this is impossible, replace [Surah al-Mulk](A71) with repeating [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty-five times.\n\nThe Twenty-Eighth Night Prayer: Six units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) one hundred times, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times, and [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) one hundred times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated one hundred times:\n\nAccording to my own readings in the books of narrations, I found that the prayer of the twenty-eighth night of Ramadan consists of six units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once, [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) ten times, [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) ten times, and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten times. After accomplishment the same invocation is repeated one hundred times.\n\nThe Twenty-Ninth Night Prayer: Two units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty times.\n\nThe Thirtieth Night Prayer: Twelve units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated one hundred times:\n\nNote that each two units of all of these prayers should be separated by uttering the Taslim statement.",
  "merits": "In Zad al-Ma’ad, ‘Allamah al-Majlisi has referred to the prayers of Ramadan nights in the last chapter of the recommended rites of Ramadan. Hereby, I will refer to these prayers as briefly as mentioned in the book involved:"
